"""Build dated parking evidence and exact GIS inventory arithmetic, without availability claims."""
import html,json
from pathlib import Path
from urllib.parse import urlencode
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'data/processed/campus-walk';esc=html.escape
t=json.loads((OUT/'talley-parking-gis-raw.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));w=json.loads((OUT/'parking-gis-raw.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));byid={f['attributes']['OBJECTID']:f['attributes'] for d in [t,w] for f in d['data']['features']}
groups=[('Coliseum Deck · deck records only',[26,92,166]),('McKimmon · four mapped lot areas',[34,38,55,56]),('Jeter Bays · separate surface parking',[143]),('Coliseum visitor area · separate surface parking',[144]),('Business Services · separate lot',[82])]
base='https://gismaps.oit.ncsu.edu/arcgis/rest/services/Transportation/Transportation_OnlineCampusMap/MapServer/1'
records=[]
for name,ids in groups:
 for oid in ids:
  a=byid[oid];url=base+'/query?'+urlencode({'where':f'OBJECTID = {oid}','outFields':'*','returnGeometry':'false','f':'pjson'})
  records.append(f'<tr><th>{esc(a["NAME"])}</th><td>{oid}</td><td>{esc(a["Type"])}</td><td>{esc(a["ZONE_"])}</td><td>{a["SPACES"]:,}</td><td><a href="{esc(url,quote=True)}">Official GIS record</a></td></tr>')
calculations=''.join('<li>'+esc(name)+': <strong>'+' + '.join(f'{byid[i]["SPACES"]:,}' for i in ids)+' = '+f'{sum(byid[i]["SPACES"] for i in ids):,}'+'</strong> mapped spaces.</li>' for name,ids in groups)
block='''<!-- BEGIN PARKING COMPARISON -->
<section id="talley-parking"><h2>Talley: Coliseum Deck and outdoor Jeter parking</h2><p>University sources confirm that both the deck and nearby outdoor bays have provided voter parking, but the evidence is election-specific:</p><ul><li><strong>2024 primary, February 15–March 2:</strong> NC State’s February 7 notice assigned Jeter Drive outdoor bays to voters without a university parking permit: the first bay February 15–27, then the first and second bays February 28–March 2. <a href="https://news.ncsu.edu/2024/02/nc-state-to-host-early-voting-site/">Official university notice</a>.</li><li><strong>2026 primary, February 12–28:</strong> NC State Transportation’s February 9 notice identified an area on Coliseum Deck’s second level for Talley early voters, using the first entrance from Jeter Drive. It did not designate the whole deck. <a href="https://transportation.ncsu.edu/2026/02/parking-information-for-early-voting-at-nc-state-february-12-28/">Official transportation notice</a>.</li></ul><p><strong>The exact fall 2022 voter-parking reservation plan has not been verified.</strong> These later-election notices are not proof of 2022 arrangements. Our map outlines five current GIS features around Talley: four Coliseum parking-zone records and Jeter Bays (OBJECTIDs 26, 92, 143, 144 and 166). They do not delineate the reserved deck level or individual reserved outdoor bays. <a href="data/sources/ncsu-gis/2026-11-01/talley-parking-query.json">Saved original GIS query</a> · <a href="data/sources/ncsu-gis/2026-11-01/parking-evidence.json">Dated evidence and limits</a>.</p></section>
<section id="parking-capacity"><h2>Parking inventory: Coliseum Deck versus McKimmon</h2><p><strong>The downloaded GIS lists 2,192 spaces in Coliseum Deck’s deck records and 660 across four McKimmon lot records.</strong> These are source-record inventory totals, not counts of vacant, voter-accessible or voter-reserved spaces. The snapshot was downloaded November 1, 2026; it does not reconstruct capacity in 2022 or establish when each inventory figure was last updated. Only designated portions were provided for voting in the dated notices above and at Western Boulevard; their exact voter-reserved counts are unverified.</p><h3>Step-by-step math</h3><p>Take the original <code>SPACES</code> field once per distinct GIS <code>OBJECTID</code>. For Coliseum Deck, include only the three records tagged <code>Type = Deck</code>: visitor pay, CD and RE parking zones. Keep the separately mapped surface visitor area and Jeter Bays outside the deck total. McKimmon includes its North and South lots plus the two private visitor-lot records; Business Services is separate. Do not estimate spaces from polygon area or multiply records by the number of floors.</p><ol>'''+calculations+'''</ol><details><summary>Every original record used in the inventory</summary><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Original GIS name</th><th>OBJECTID</th><th>Type</th><th>Zone</th><th>SPACES</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(records)+'''</tbody></table></div></details><h3>A hypothetical 660-space allotment at Coliseum</h3><p>Using the GIS-listed totals, an allotment of 660 spaces at Coliseum Deck would account for <strong>30.1%</strong> of its inventory and leave <strong>1,532 spaces (69.9%)</strong> outside that hypothetical allotment.</p><ol><li>660 ÷ 2,192 × 100 = 30.109…%, rounded to <strong>30.1%</strong>.</li><li>2,192 − 660 = <strong>1,532</strong> spaces.</li><li>1,532 ÷ 2,192 × 100 = 69.890…%, rounded to <strong>69.9%</strong>.</li></ol><p>This is a scale comparison, not evidence that 660 spaces could operationally be reserved, that the other spaces were vacant, or that either site actually had this allotment. Existing permit commitments, occupancy, accessible-space needs and election-day operational arrangements are not established by these inventory records.</p><h3>How many McKimmon spaces were reserved for voting?</h3><p><strong>Not confirmed from the public sources reviewed.</strong> NC State Transportation’s October 9, 2026 notice identifies a reserved portion of McKimmon and a separate accessible-parking area, but gives no numerical allotment. Pack the Polls likewise identifies designated McKimmon areas without a count. The GIS <code>SPACES</code> field describes the full parking-zone record, not the highlighted voter subsection. We therefore do not label 660, either private-lot subtotal, or a visually estimated count as the actual voter allocation. Confirming it would require a dated election parking-allocation plan or a count from NC State Transportation or Wake County Elections. <a href="https://transportation.ncsu.edu/2026/10/early-voting-at-nc-state-october-15-31/">Official reservation notice</a> · <a href="https://packthepolls.dasa.ncsu.edu/elections/early-voting/">University voter-parking guidance</a>. The original university map was visually reviewed: it marks the general and accessible areas but prints no numerical allotment.</p><details><summary>View the saved official reserved-parking map</summary><a href="data/sources/ncsu-gis/2026-11-01/Voting-Reserved-Spaces.jpg"><img src="data/sources/ncsu-gis/2026-11-01/Voting-Reserved-Spaces.jpg" width="600" height="391" style="max-width:100%;height:auto" loading="lazy" alt="Original NC State Transportation plan: red general voter-parking subsection beside Western Boulevard Business Services and separate blue ADA parking. No numerical space count is printed."></a><p>Source: NC State Transportation, October 9, 2026. Preserved original image; no boundary or count was added.</p></details><h3>Why this is labeled GIS inventory</h3><p>Other university publications use different McKimmon figures: a <a href="https://jobs.ncsu.edu/postings/230214">university job description</a> describes 650 spaces, while a <a href="https://olli.lifelonglearning.ncsu.edu/2025/01/olli-is-a-community-2/">January 2025 OLLI notice</a> describes more than 700. The sources do not establish why these figures differ. We therefore retain one reproducible GIS definition for both locations and disclose the disagreement, rather than present a verified current physical capacity. The GIS field includes different parking-use categories, including marked motorcycle allocations, and does not establish permission to park; these are not independently audited car-only capacities.</p><p>Similarly, <a href="https://transportation.ncsu.edu/visitor-parking/">Transportation’s visitor-parking page</a> lists 331 spaces for Coliseum’s lower-level pay lot; that is a visitor subset, not the whole deck, and differs from the downloaded visitor-zone records. Neither that subset nor the full deck total is a confirmed voter allotment. These figures cannot establish which site had more parking available specifically for voters.</p><p><a href="data/sources/ncsu-gis/2026-11-01/talley-parking-query.json">Original Coliseum/Jeter records</a> · <a href="data/sources/ncsu-gis/2026-11-01/parking-query.json">Original McKimmon-area records</a> · <a href="data/processed/campus-walk/nearby-parking.geojson">All ten displayed GIS polygons and counts</a> · <a href="data/sources/ncsu-gis/2026-11-01/catalog.json">Snapshot hashes</a>.</p><p>Display markers are centered on each GIS building outline’s bounding box. Route endpoints, route distances, proximity calculations and averages retain the original GIS entrance points. This is a visual change only. Both maps have a collapsible floating key; route hover tooltips identify the displayed trip. Several trips can share the same path, so a tooltip identifies the topmost displayed route rather than every trip using that segment.</p></section>
<!-- END PARKING COMPARISON -->'''
p=ROOT/'report-source/article-references.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');start='<!-- BEGIN PARKING COMPARISON -->';end='<!-- END PARKING COMPARISON -->'
if start in s:
 a=s.index(start);b=s.index(end,a)+len(end);s=s[:a]+block+s[b:]
else:s=s.replace('<section id="gis-archive">',block+'\n<section id="gis-archive">')
s=s.replace(' Checking Show all routes pauses autoplay and restores the full route network.','')
s=s.replace('The camera fits the full eligible route area once when playback starts, then remains fixed between routes.', 'The camera fits the full eligible route area once when playback starts, then remains fixed between routes. Checking Show all routes pauses autoplay and restores the full route network.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8');print('Built dated Talley parking evidence and exact 2,192 vs 660 GIS inventory with exclusions and source disagreements.')
